  "headphonesNote": "Binaural beats require stereo headphones to work.",
  "attuneIntroKicker1": "Frequencies",
  "attuneIntroTitle1": "Two tones, one in each ear",
  "attuneIntroBody1": "A binaural beat is two steady tones. The left ear hears one frequency. The right ear hears a frequency a few hertz away. The pulse you notice is that difference. It is not a separate tone in the sound. Hearing builds it, and only when each ear receives its own tone.\n\nStereo headphones are required. Speakers, or a single earbud, let both tones into both ears. Then there is no binaural beat.\n\nIsochronic tones are the other choice. One tone is pulsed at the beat rate. They work on speakers, and they can feel sharper.",
  "attuneIntroKicker2": "Before you listen",
  "attuneIntroTitle2": "Hemispheric sound is strong",
  "attuneIntroBody2": "Each ear sends its tone along its own path. That split is what people mean by hemispheric synchronization. The bands name the beat rate, not a promise. Delta is about 2 Hz, theta about 6, alpha about 10, and beta about 20. The carrier, from 100 to 400 Hz, is the pitch you hear.\n\nThis app does not read your brain, and it does not place you in a state. Sit or lie down somewhere you can stop. Do not use this while driving, in water, or when your attention is needed elsewhere. Keep the volume comfortable. The sound rises over the first moment. Stop if you feel dizzy, tense, or unwell. If you have a history of seizures, skip this tool.",
  "attuneIntroFootnote": "This is not treatment, and it is not EMDR. The Anchor stays available.",
  "attuneIntroUnderstand": "I understand",
  "attuneIntroAgain": "About these frequencies",
  "attuneWaiverTitle": "Before the tones",
  "attuneWaiverRecorded": "This choice is stored on this device.",
  "attuneWaiverSeizure": "I do not have a history of epilepsy or seizure disorders.",
  "attuneWaiverMachinery": "I will not operate heavy machinery or drive while listening.",
  "attuneWaiverRisk": "I assume all risks associated with brainwave entrainment, releasing the creators from liability regarding adverse psychiatric reactions.",
  "attuneWaiverEnter": "Enter",
  "attuneCarouselAccept": "I Understand and Accept",
  "attuneToneLevel": "Tone",
